 "intro": {
  "title": "ASH BASILICA",
  "lines": [
   "A house of the Song, burned out and kept.",
   "Five stations down the nave. At each one, someone who wants the Grafting to go on."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "Behind the altar a stair goes down. The ash on it has been walked by many feet, all going the same way.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [30, 124],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Ash on the flags, soot to the roof and a long nave of five bays in a row. Everything that can burn has. The stone is still warm at the foot of the walls."
  },
  {
   "id": "raised",
   "at": [30, 117],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The aisles are two metres up, and the ramps through the pillars are the only ways onto them. High ground costs a flight of steps and gives the nave in front of you."
  },
  {
   "id": "haul",
   "at": [30, 106],
   "radius": 4,
